nd docstring from the problem text.",\n            context=self.problem_text\n        )\n\n        # Step 2: Analyze the docstring to understand the problem requirements\n        docstring_analysis = await self.generate(\n            instruction=f"Analyze the docstring to understand the problem requirements. "\n                        f"Identify the inputs, outputs, and any specific constraints or edge cases mentioned.",\n            context=function_signature\n        )\n\n        # Step 3: Generate an initial implementation based on the analysis\n        initial_implementation = await self.generate(\n            instruction=f"Based on the analysis of the docstring, generate an initial implementation "\n                        f"of the function. Ensure that the implementation adheres to the function signature "\n                        f"and handles all edge cases mentioned in the docstring.",\n            context=docstring_analysis\n        )\n\n        # Step 4: Revise the implementation to improve clarity, correctness, and efficiency\n        revised_implementation = await self.revise(\n            instruction="Critique and refine the implementation to ensure it is clear, correct, and efficient. "\n                        "Check for any potential bugs or inefficiencies and make necessary improvements.",\n            context=initial_implementation\n        )\n\n        # Step 5: Summarize the final implementation\n        final_implementation = await self.summarize(\n            instruction="Condense the final implementation into a concise and well-documented Python function "\n                        "that matches the function signature and satisfies all requirements in the docstring.",\n            context=revised_implementation\n        )\n\n        # Step 6: Return the final implementation\n        return final_implementation\n```', '<think>\n</think>\n\n</think>\n\n```python\n# --- DO NOT IMPORT HERE ---\nclass Workflow:\n    def __init__(self, config, probl