estion. \n        Ensure each candidate answer is supported by the provided context documents. \n        Format the output as a list of candidate answers with brief explanations.\n        """\n        candidates = await self.generate(instruction=candidate_answers_instruction, context=self.problem_text)\n\n        # Step 4: Refine and critique the candidate answers\n        refinement_instruction = """\n        Critique the candidate answers for accuracy, completeness, and relevance. \n        Ensure each answer is supported by the context documents and aligns with the reasoning chain. \n        Provide a refined version of each candidate answer.\n        """\n        refined_answers = await self.revise(instruction=refinement_instruction, context=candidates)\n\n        # Step 5: Ensemble the refined answers to select the best one\n        ensemble_instruction = """\n        Evaluate the refined answers and select the best one based on accuracy, clarity, and relevance. \n        If multiple answers are equally valid, provide a synthesis of the best aspects of each.\n        """\n        final_answer = await self.ensemble(instruction=ensemble_instruction, contexts=refined_answers)\n\n        return final_answer\n```', '<think>\n</think>\n\n</think>\n\n```python\n# --- DO NOT IMPORT HERE ---\nclass Workflow:\n    def __init__(self, config, problem) -> None:\n        # --- DO NOT MODIFY THIS SECTION ---\n        self.config = config\n        self.problem_text = problem\n        self.llm = create(config)\n        \n        self.generate = operator.Generate(self.llm, self.problem_text)\n        self.revise = operator.Revise(self.llm, self.problem_text)\n        self.summarize = operator.Summarize(self.llm, self.problem_text)\n        self.ensemble = operator.Ensemble(self.llm, self.problem_text)\n\n    async def run_workflow(self):\n        """\n        Implement the core problem-solving logic here.\n        Remember: \n        - Use detailed, comprehensive instructions\n 