tion named \'{func_name}\' that solves the task described in the problem. \n            Requirements:\n            1. Include ALL necessary import statements at the top.\n            2. Handle edge cases such as empty inputs, None values, and boundary conditions.\n            3. Ensure the function signature matches the test cases provided.\n            4. Return ONLY the executable Python code, without any explanations or additional text.\n            """,\n            context=self.problem_text\n        )\n\n        # Step 3: Revise the initial code to ensure correctness and completeness\n        revised_code = await self.revise(\n            instruction="""\n            Review the provided Python code and ensure it meets the following criteria:\n            1. The function signature matches the test cases.\n            2. All edge cases are handled appropriately.\n            3. The code is clean, efficient, and follows Pythonic best practices.\n            4. All necessary import statements are included.\n            5. The code passes the test cases provided in the problem description.\n            Return ONLY the corrected and improved Python code, without any explanations or additional text.\n            """,\n            context=initial_code\n        )\n\n        # Step 4: Ensemble to select the best version of the code\n        final_code = await self.ensemble(\n            instruction="""\n            Evaluate the following candidate solutions and select the best one:\n            1. The initial implementation of the function.\n            2. The revised version of the function.\n            Criteria for selection:\n            - Correctness: Does the code pass the test cases?\n            - Completeness: Are all edge cases handled?\n            - Efficiency: Is the code optimized for performance?\n            - Readability: Is the code clean and easy to understand?\n            Return ONLY the selected Python code, without any explanations or additional te