s such as empty inputs, None, and boundary values.\n            3. Return ONLY the executable Python code, no explanations.\n            """,\n            context=self.problem_text\n        )\n\n        # Step 3: Revise the initial code for correctness and completeness\n        revised_code = await self.revise(\n            instruction="""\n            Review the provided Python code and ensure it meets the following criteria:\n            1. Correctly implements the task described in the problem.\n            2. Handles all edge cases and special scenarios.\n            3. Includes all necessary import statements.\n            4. Returns the correct output format as specified.\n            Fix any issues and return ONLY the corrected code.\n            """,\n            context=initial_code\n        )\n\n        # Step 4: Ensemble to decide between initial and revised code\n        final_code = await self.ensemble(\n            instruction="""\n            Evaluate the following two candidate solutions:\n            1. Initial Code: {initial_code}\n            2. Revised Code: {revised_code}\n            \n            Select the best solution based on the following criteria:\n            - Correctness of implementation\n            - Handling of edge cases\n            - Efficiency and Pythonic style\n            - Completeness of the solution\n            \n            Return ONLY the selected code.\n            """,\n            contexts=[initial_code, revised_code]\n        )\n\n        return final_code\n```', '<think>\n</think>\n\n</think>\n\n```python\n# --- DO NOT IMPORT HERE ---\nclass Workflow:\n    def __init__(self, config, problem) -> None:\n        # --- DO NOT MODIFY THIS SECTION ---\n        self.config = config\n        self.problem_text = problem\n        self.llm = create(config)\n        \n        self.generate = operator.Generate(self.llm, self.problem_text)\n        self.revise = operator.Revise(self.llm, self.problem_text)\n        self.summar