 as empty inputs, None, and boundary values.\n            3. Ensure the function signature matches the test cases.\n            4. Return ONLY the executable Python code, no explanations.\n            """,\n            context=self.problem_text\n        )\n\n        # Step 3: Revise the initial code for correctness and completeness\n        revised_code = await self.revise(\n            instruction="""\n            Review the following Python code and make any necessary improvements:\n            - Ensure all edge cases are handled.\n            - Check for missing imports.\n            - Verify that the function signature matches the test cases.\n            - Ensure the code is efficient and follows Python best practices.\n            Return ONLY the corrected Python code, no explanations.\n            """,\n            context=initial_code\n        )\n\n        # Step 4: Ensemble to decide between the initial and revised code\n        final_code = await self.ensemble(\n            instruction="""\n            Evaluate the following two versions of the Python function:\n            - Version 1: {initial_code}\n            - Version 2: {revised_code}\n            \n            Select the best version based on the following criteria:\n            - Correctness of the implementation\n            - Handling of edge cases\n            - Efficiency and Pythonic style\n            - Matching the function signature with the test cases\n            \n            Return ONLY the selected Python code, no explanations.\n            """,\n            contexts=[initial_code, revised_code]\n        )\n\n        return final_code\n```', '<think>\n</think>\n\n</think>\n\n```python\n# --- DO NOT IMPORT HERE ---\nclass Workflow:\n    def __init__(self, config, problem) -> None:\n        # --- DO NOT MODIFY THIS SECTION ---\n        self.config = config\n        self.problem_text = problem\n        self.llm = create(config)\n        \n        self.generate = operator.Generate(self.ll